$grp PS_MissionDescription : "{3136BE42592F3B1B}PrefabsEditable/MissionDescription/EditableMissionDescription.et" {
 SIT {
  coords 345.619 36.85 7375.71
  m_sTitle "Situation"
  m_sTextData "<h2>PRELIMS</h2>"\
  "DTL: 21/07/1991, 0600hrs, Northern Ireland."\
  "Weather: Clear, light winds, visibility 1km+, with forecast of change."\
  ""\
  "<h2>LORE</h2>"\
  "Operation Banner remains ongoing as British forces continue to support the Royal Ulster Constabulary in maintaining security and disrupting paramilitary activity across Northern Ireland."\
  ""\
  "Over recent months, IRA personnel have repeatedly used three isolated farmyards overlooking the Main Supply Route (MSR) between Lovetin and Kamoryn to conduct ambushes against British Army patrols, Royal Ulster Constabulary units, and, on occasion, civilian traffic. The locations are not permanently occupied, with personnel moving in and out using irregular patterns to avoid detection."\
  ""\
  "Following weeks of surveillance and intelligence gathering, C Company has been tasked with conducting a coordinated search operation to clear the suspected locations, deny the IRA use of the farmyards, and restore freedom of movement along the route."
  m_aVisibleForFactions {
   "UK"
  }
  m_iOrder 1
 }
 CS {
  coords 345.619 36.85 7375.71
  m_sTitle "Comsig"
  m_sTextData "<h2>CALLSIGNS</h2>"\
  "• PHQ - 22"\
  "• PLT OC - 22A"\
  "• PSGT - 22B"\
  "• 1 SEC - 22C"\
  "• 2 SEC - 22D"\
  ""\
  "• TRP OC/1st vehicle - 31A"\
  "• TRP SGT/2nd vehicle - 31B"\
  "• 3rd vehicle - 31C"\
  "• 4th vehicle - 31D"\
  ""\
  "<h2>FREQ/CHAN</h2>"\
  "• Joint net - 48.2Mhz"\
  "• Platoon net - 48.0Mhz"\
  "• Troop net - 49.8Mhz"\
  ""\
  "<h2>PASSWORDS</h2>"\
  "All can be changed at CO's discretion."\
  "• <b>Challenge:</b> Royal | <b>Password:</b> Digger"\
  "• Running password: 75"
  m_aVisibleForFactions {
   "UK"
  }
  m_iOrder 5
 }
 EF {
  coords 345.619 36.85 7375.71
  m_sTitle "Enemy forces"
  m_sTextData "<h2>COMPOSITION & DISPOSITION</h2>  "\
  "Enemy forces consist of the Irish Republican Army (IRA), operating throughout the marked area of operations. Intelligence estimates enemy strength up to 35 personnel. This assessment is based on close target reconnaissance of ambush sites, reports from British and Garda convoys, and information provided by the local population."\
  ""\
  "<h2>STRENGTHS & CAPABILITIES</h2> "\
  "• Reports from convoys indicate the IRA has employed heavy machine guns from elevated positions providing effective fields of fire over the MSR."\
  "• Regular use of explosive charges and booby traps."\
  "• Knowledge of the local terrain and established ambush positions particularly overlooking the MSR and its key approaches."\
  "• Expect a lightly equipped but highly mobile force capable of conducting well-coordinated hit-and-run engagements before breaking contact."
  m_aVisibleForFactions {
   "UK"
  }
  m_iOrder 2
 }
 FF {
  coords 345.619 36.85 7375.71
  m_sTitle "Friendly forces"
  m_sTextData "<h2>COMPOSITION & DISPOSITION</h2>  "\
  "We are the British Army."\
  "Consisting of light infantry from 2 Platoon(-), B Company, 2nd Battalion, Royal Green Jackets (2 RGJ), with a strength of 20 personnel. Attached in support is 1 Troop, C Squadron, Royal Yeomanry, consisting of 12 personnel."\
  "Both elements are currently staged at GRID: 022059"\
  ""\
  "<h2>STRENGTHS & CAPABILITIES</h2>  "\
  "• High mobility provided by the attached light cavalry troop, operating 4x WMIKs equipped with roof-mounted .50 cal heavy machine guns and front-mounted GPMGs."\
  "• Light infantry supported by mobile direct fire assets, allowing rapid manoeuvre between objectives."\
  ""\
  "<h2>SERVICE & SUPPORT</h2>  "\
  "• None."
  m_aVisibleForFactions {
   "UK"
  }
  m_iOrder 3
 }
 MIS {
  coords 345.619 36.85 7375.71
  m_sTitle "Mission"
  m_sTextData "<h2>MISSION STATEMENT</h2>  "\
  "We are to conduct a <b>DELIBERATE ATTACK</b> in order to <b>SWEEP</b> Objectives Dog and Cat before <b>SECURING</b> Objective Bird by clearing and holding."\
  ""\
  "<h2>MISSION DESCRIPTION</h2>  "\
  "IRA personnel have been using the farmyards along this route to conduct irregular ambushes against British Army and Garda patrols travelling between Lovetin and Kamoryn. Their attacks have also placed civilian traffic at risk, with several non-combatants caught in the crossfire."\
  ""\
  "Following weeks of intelligence gathering and terrain analysis, these three farmyards have been identified as the most likely staging and ambush locations. Their concealed positions, restricted approaches, and commanding views over the MSR make them ideal for hit-and-run attacks."\
  ""\
  "Our mission is to sweep Objectives Dog and Cat for enemy personnel and materiel before securing Objective Bird, denying the IRA further use of these positions and restoring freedom of movement along the route."
  m_aVisibleForFactions {
   "UK"
  }
  m_iOrder 4
 }
}